# Kaggle submission — agents must NOT submit

**Cursor agents, subagents, and automation must NEVER submit to Kaggle unless the user explicitly asks in that conversation** (e.g. "submit to Kaggle", "run kaggle competitions submit").

## Forbidden without explicit user request

- Running `scripts/smoke_and_submit.sh` (even with `--submit`)
- Running `kaggle competitions submit`
- Any script, Makefile target, or CI step that uploads a submission bundle
- Treating "verify", "test plan", "rebuild", or plan todo "resubmit" as permission to submit

## Allowed for agents (local only)

- `scripts/smoke_test.sh` — build tarball + local 720-step smoke test
- Inline `kaggle_environments` smoke: `make("kaggriculture", ...); env.run([...])`
- Building `submission.tar.gz` without uploading (if the user asked to build the bundle)

## When the user explicitly asks to submit

- Run `scripts/smoke_and_submit.sh --submit "their message"` (not the smoke-only script)
- Or run `kaggle competitions submit` with the path and message they specify
- Do not submit on your own initiative after fixes, smoke passes, or completed plans

## Humans

Users may run `scripts/smoke_and_submit.sh --submit "message"` locally anytime.
